{"seq":6,"slug":"franklin-roosevelt-legacy","title":"富兰克林·罗斯福：历史影响与评价","stage":"DONE","category":"franklin-roosevelt","categoryLabel":"富兰克林·罗斯福","chapterCount":3,"docCount":7,"url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy","rating":{"composite":3.77,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.6,"coverage":2.5,"positioning":null,"strategic":5},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":null},"hubDir":"/Users/wangyang.learnwy/learnwy/learnwy/l-doc-hub/hubs/leaders/11_franklin-roosevelt/6_franklin-roosevelt-legacy","introMarkdown":"# 富兰克林·罗斯福：历史影响与评价\n\n富兰克林·德拉诺·罗斯福（Franklin Delano Roosevelt，1882—1945）是美国历史上唯一连任四届、在任时间最长的总统，从 1933 年 3 月就职到 1945 年 4 月在佐治亚州沃姆斯普林斯（Warm Springs）病逝，他执政超过十二年。这十二年横跨大萧条与第二次世界大战两场二十世纪最严重的危机，也正因如此，对罗斯福的评价无法绕开一个核心问题：在国家陷入存亡关头时，一位总统能在多大程度上重塑制度、重排世界格局，又应当为此承担怎样的责任。\n\n本知识库不复述罗斯福的生平年表，而是聚焦\"遗产\"与\"评价\"——即他在 1945 年去世之后，仍持续塑造美国与世界的那些结构性后果。这是一个争议性极强的题目：在西恩纳学院（Siena College）等机构反复进行的总统排名中，罗斯福长期与林肯、华盛顿并列前三，2022 年的西恩纳调查甚至将他排在第一位；但与此同时，他签署的第 9066 号行政命令导致约十二万日裔美国人被强制拘禁，雅尔塔会议上对东欧的安排被批评为\"出卖\"，最高法院改组计划则被视为对宪政制衡的危险冲击。\n\n本库分为三个章节。第一章考察国内制度遗产：新政（New Deal）如何把一个有限政府的国家改造为拥有社会保障、存款保险、证券监管与劳工权利的现代行政国家，以及\"帝王般的现代总统职位\"的成型。第二章转向国际秩序：从战时大同盟、雅尔塔与德黑兰的首脑外交，到布雷顿森林体系与联合国的设计，再到美国由孤立主义走向超级大国的身份转变。第三章直面史学评价与争议，梳理罗斯福\"伟大\"叙事的依据，也不回避其统治中的黑暗篇章。\n\n阅读本库不需要预先具备美国史背景。我们会标注关键的日期、地点、人物与原始文献（如 1933 年首次就职演说、四大自由演说、各项立法名称），力求在事实准确的前提下呈现一种平衡、中立的参考视角，让读者能够自己判断：罗斯福究竟是拯救了资本主义与民主制度的改革者，还是过度扩张联邦权力、留下诸多隐患的争议人物——抑或两者兼而有之。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"domestic-and-institutional-legacy","title":"国内制度遗产与现代美国的塑造","docCount":2,"url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy/domestic-and-institutional-legacy","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"new-deal-and-modern-state","title":"新政与现代行政国家的缔造","url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy/domestic-and-institutional-legacy/new-deal-and-modern-state"},{"seq":2,"slug":"social-and-economic-institutions","title":"幸存至今的社会与经济制度","url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy/domestic-and-institutional-legacy/social-and-economic-institutions"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"international-order-and-global-influence","title":"国际秩序与全球影响","docCount":3,"url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy/international-order-and-global-influence","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"wartime-leadership-and-grand-alliance","title":"战时领导与大同盟外交","url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy/international-order-and-global-influence/wartime-leadership-and-grand-alliance"},{"seq":2,"slug":"postwar-international-architecture","title":"战后国际架构：联合国与布雷顿森林体系","url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy/international-order-and-global-influence/postwar-international-architecture"},{"seq":3,"slug":"american-superpower-and-global-image","title":"美国超级大国地位与全球形象的塑造","url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy/international-order-and-global-influence/american-superpower-and-global-image"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"historiography-and-controversies","title":"史学评价与争议","docCount":2,"url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy/historiography-and-controversies","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"greatness-and-presidential-rankings","title":"\"伟大\"叙事与总统排名","url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy/historiography-and-controversies/greatness-and-presidential-rankings"},{"seq":2,"slug":"criticisms-and-dark-chapters","title":"批评与黑暗篇章","url":"/c/leaders/franklin-roosevelt/franklin-roosevelt-legacy/historiography-and-controversies/criticisms-and-dark-chapters"}]}]}